hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19648","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Hisham, Qatadah narrated to us from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad from Madan ibn Abi Talhah from Abu Najih al-Sulami, he said: We besieged with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the fortress of Taif, or the palace of Taif, and he said: Whoever reaches with an arrow in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic, then for him is a rank in Paradise. I reached that day sixteen arrows. And whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic, it is for him equal to freeing a slave. And whoever is afflicted with grey hair in the path of Allah Mighty and Majestic, it is for him a light on the Day of Resurrection. And whatever man frees a Muslim man, Allah Mighty and Majestic makes the protection of every bone of his bones a bone of the bones of his freer from the Fire. And whatever Muslim woman frees a Muslim woman, Allah Mighty and Majestic makes the protection of every bone of her bones a bone of the bones of her freer from the Fire."
"19649","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us from Said from Qatadah from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad al-Ghatafani from Madan ibn Abi Talhah al-Yamuri from Abu Najih al-Sulami, he said: We besieged with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the fortress of Taif, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah and it reaches, then for him is a rank in Paradise. A man said: O Prophet of Allah, if I shoot and reach, is there for me a rank in Paradise. He said: So he shot and reached. He said: I reached that day sixteen arrows, then he mentioned its meaning."
